  - multiscale feature fusion
  - HAM10000
  - ISIC
license: MIT
abstract: >
  We propose a dermoscopic skin lesion classification framework built on a
  DINOv3-pretrained ConvNeXt-B backbone augmented with three novel modules:
  Lesion Aware Dual Attention (LADA), Adaptive Dilated Scale Fusion (ADSF),
  and Cross-Scale Gated Aggregation (CSGA). Training uses a class-balanced
  adaptive-margin loss with five-fold lesion-grouped cross-validation on
  HAM10000, achieving 99.36% accuracy and 99.01% macro F1. External
  validation is performed on ISIC 2017, PAD-UFES-20, and BCN20000.
